  <!-- Marker set of the University of Bath running dataset (dynamic and static-trial markers; treadmill corner markers omitted). Positions of cluster, foot and static-only markers are medians over the 50 static trials (both sides), mapped into the model by per-segment similarity fits on the epicondyle, malleolus, calcaneus and fifth-metatarsal markers. These fitted positions are generated by scripts/fit_markersets_bath.py from the published static trials; citation, method and fit residuals are in myo_sim/build/data/markersets_bath.json.
       Sources:
         Carter J, Chen X, Cazzola D, Trewartha G, Preatoni E (2024) Full Body Kinematics and Ground Reaction Forces of Fifty Heterogeneous Runners Completing Treadmill Running at Various Speeds and Gradients. University of Bath. https://doi.org/10.15125/BATH-01341
         Marker names and placement: MarkerSet_Info.docx of that dataset, https://researchdata.bath.ac.uk/1341/
       Optional overlay: myo_sim.markersets.add_markerset(spec, "bath_running") adds these sites to the bodies of the same
       name. Positions are in body frames (x anterior, y up, z right). The class gives the confidence of the position:
       anatomical (on a model landmark site), reference (from a published model with the same body frames),
       fitted (fitted to recorded data), nominal (from the written placement description). -->
  <default>
    <default class="myomarker">
      <site type="sphere" size="0.008" group="4"/>
      <default class="myomarker_anatomical"><site rgba="0.2 0.6 1 1"/></default>
      <default class="myomarker_reference"><site rgba="0.2 0.8 0.4 1"/></default>
      <default class="myomarker_fitted"><site rgba="1 0.7 0.1 1"/></default>
      <default class="myomarker_nominal"><site rgba="0.9 0.3 0.3 1"/></default>
    </default>
  </default>
